  "Notes": [
    {
      "Text": "libsoup security update",
      "Title": "Synopsis",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "An update for libsoup is now available for openEuler-22.03-LTS-SP4",
      "Title": "Summary",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "libsoup is an HTTP client/server library for GNOME. It uses GObjects and the glib main loop, to integrate well with GNOME applications, and also has a synchronous API, for use in threaded applications.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nSoupAuthManager caches proxy authentication credentials without scoping them to the proxy authority (host:port). When the proxy configuration changes (e.g., via system settings or WPAD), cached Proxy-Authorization headers from the previous proxy are sent to the new proxy, leaking credentials.(CVE-2026-12547)",
      "Title": "Description",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "An update for libsoup is now available for openEuler-22.03-LTS-SP4.\n\nopenEuler Security has rated this update as having a security impact of low. A Common Vunlnerability Scoring System(CVSS)base score,which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVElink(s) in the References section.",
      "Title": "Topic",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "Low",
      "Title": "Severity",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "libsoup",
      "Title": "Affected Component",
      "Type": "General"
    }
  ],
